raw:
That the applicant, [NAME OF APPLICANT], is a person having a direct and pecuniary interest in the subject matter of the pending suit and therefore is a necessary party within the meaning of the Code of Civil Procedure, 1908;  

That the continuation of the suit without the presence of the applicant would risk a multiplicity of proceedings and may result in a decree that is not binding upon the applicant, contrary to the principles of justice and equity;  

That the applicant seeks to be impleaded as an intervener pursuant to the provisions of the Code of Civil Procedure, 1908, which empower the Court to add a necessary party to ensure that all interests affected by the suit are adequately represented;  

That the applicant’s inclusion as a necessary party will enable the Court to adjudicate the dispute comprehensively and avoid any future litigation on the same cause of action;  

That the applicant is ready to comply with any directions of the Court, including furnishing security, filing an address for service, and bearing costs as may be ordered.  

[placeholder] (CPC provision governing addition of necessary parties).

